================================================================================
1. CORE PURPOSE AND PHILOSOPHY
================================================================================
DotRec is developed as a completely free, convenient, ad-free, watermark-free,
and privacy-respecting screen recording application for Android.

The source code is published openly on GitHub for public transparency, security
auditing, learning, community contributions, and personal compilation.

To safeguard users against fraudulent clones, scam apps, injected malware,
ad-supported forks, paywalled repackages, and unauthorized marketplace exploitation,
DISTRIBUTION OF THE SOFTWARE TO ANY APPLICATION STORE OR DIGITAL MARKETPLACE
IS EXCLUSIVELY RESERVED FOR THE COPYRIGHT HOLDER.

================================================================================
2. PERMITTED USES (GRANT OF RIGHTS)
================================================================================
Subject to the terms and limitations set forth in this License, the Copyright
Holder grants to any person obtaining a copy of this software and associated
documentation files (the "Software"), free of charge, the non-exclusive right to:

  (a) View, read, inspect, audit, study, and research the source code;
  (b) Make personal modifications, bug fixes, enhancements, and submit pull
      requests or issues back to the official DotRec repository;
  (c) Compile and build executable binaries (e.g. APKs) locally on your own
      machine solely for your own personal, private, non-commercial use on your
      own personal devices;
  (d) Share unmodified or modified source code strictly in source-code form
      (such as public forks on GitHub), provided that:
        (i)  This LICENSE file and all copyright notices remain fully intact;
        (ii) It is made explicitly clear that the fork is not the official
             DotRec application.

